course: dictionary
lesson: 3265
title: Equity: fair chances for everyone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Equity means fairness. It is not the same as equality. «Equality gives everyone the same; equity gives each person what they need to have the same chance.»
explain: Think about glasses. «Equity gives each person what they need to have the same chance, like glasses for the child who cannot see the board.» Every child gets a fair chance to read the board, even though not every child gets the same thing.
explain: The word also has money meanings. Home equity is the part of a house that you truly own: its value minus the money you still owe. Keep the clue «treating people so each has what they need» in mind, and you will remember that equity is about fair needs, not identical gifts.
fact: Equity means fairness: giving each person what they need so they have a fair chance.
fact: Equality means everyone gets the same thing. Equity means each person gets what they need.
fact: Home equity is the part of a house's value that the owner really owns: the price minus what is still owed on the mortgage.
fact: A house worth 300 thousand pounds with 200 thousand pounds still owed has 100 thousand pounds of equity.
fact: Equities are shares in companies. Negative equity means owing more than the house is worth.
exercise: «Equality gives everyone the same; equity gives each person what they need to have the same chance.» What does equity mean? | *Fairness, giving each person what they need | Giving everyone exactly the same thing | Money kept in a bank | Having no rules at all
exercise: A school builds a ramp so a wheelchair user can join in. Which word fits best? | *Equity | Equities | Equality | Negative equity
exercise: A house is worth 300 thousand pounds and you still owe 200 thousand pounds on the mortgage. How much home equity do you have? | *100 thousand pounds | 500 thousand pounds | 300 thousand pounds | 200 thousand pounds
test: «Fairness means no favourites; it does not always mean everyone gets the same.» What does this tell you about equity? | Equity means having favourites | Equity means everyone gets exactly the same, always | Equity means a sunny day at the seaside | *Equity gives people what they need so the chances are fair
test: In money talk, what are equities? | *Shares in companies | Debts still owed on a mortgage | Houses that people rent out | Rules that judges must follow
exam: Mia's school gives extra reading help to some children so that everyone can join in. Which word fits best? | Equities | *Equity | Equality | Negative equity
